# Autonomous Sprint Runbook — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

Ready-to-copy commands for launching Claude Code as an autonomous sprint runner.
The shell is **{{SHELL}}** (default: PowerShell on Windows). All commands assume the project
directory:

```
{{PROJECT_DIR}}
```

Verify your tool versions with `claude --help` before unattended runs.

The model needs no conversational memory across runs: the **repo is the memory**
(`docs/develop/SPRINTS.md` = plan, `AGENT_PROGRESS.md` = handoff, git = state).

---

## 0. Initial setup (once)

```powershell
# 0.1 Go to the project
cd {{PROJECT_DIR}}

# 0.2 Authenticate Claude Code (subscription account). Run once, /login if prompted, then exit.
#     Do NOT set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in subscription mode.
claude

# 0.3 Start local infrastructure (database, cache, etc.) — needed for tests/migrations.
#     Skip if no local infrastructure is required for this project.
{{DB_VERIFY}}

# 0.4 Install dependencies (first time / after pull)
{{PACKAGE_MANAGER}} install

# 0.5 (Recommended) commit the planning scaffold so the agent starts from a clean base
git checkout -b chore/autonomous-setup
git add -A
git commit -m "chore: autonomous execution scaffold + sprint plan"
```

> Pre-launch check: `docs/develop/SPRINTS.md` must have exactly one sprint at
> `Status: ACTIVE` (Sprint 01) and Batch 01 at `Status: READY`.

