## 4. Permissions and security (read before unattended runs)

A headless run **cannot respond to permission prompts** — without a non-interactive mode it hangs.
`--dangerously-skip-permissions` removes all prompts. Compensating controls (enforced by the
protocol): work only on `{{BRANCH_PREFIX}}` branches, **never push to `main`/`develop`**,
no destructive DB operations (`migrate reset`, `DROP`), no deploys, no secret exposure —
all of these are human gates.

Safer alternatives (edit `$PermissionFlag` in the script, or change the flag):

| Goal | Use | Trade-off |
|---|---|---|
| Zero prompts (unattended) | `--dangerously-skip-permissions` | No OS-level barrier; relies on protocol gates + git |
| Auto-accept edits only | `--permission-mode acceptEdits` | Bash (package manager/git/docker) still prompts → may hang overnight |
| Curated allowlist | Pre-approve safe Bash in `.claude/settings.json`, run `--permission-mode default` | New commands still prompt |

Run unattended work only in this dedicated repo; the agent must never touch other directories.

