## 6. Stop

```powershell
# If running in the foreground window: press  Ctrl + C

# If detached (using the PID captured in §1):
Stop-Process -Id <PID>

# In case a hung claude process needs killing:
Get-Process claude -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Stop-Process -Force

# Stop local infrastructure when fully done (preserves data; use 'down -v' only to delete volumes)
docker compose stop
```

Stopping mid-batch is safe: progress is committed per batch and recorded in `AGENT_PROGRESS.md`;
relaunching the watchdog resumes from there.

---

## 7. How the three rules work

1. **Work until blocked** — the Execution Loop in `AGENT_EXECUTION_PROTOCOL.md` runs batch by batch.
2. **If blocked, do other available work** — the *Blocked-but-not-idle* rule: a non-quota block
   marks that batch as `BLOCKED` and the agent moves to the next batch whose dependencies are
   `DONE`; it only stops when nothing is workable.
3. **On usage limits: save, stop, resume** — the agent saves progress and exits cleanly; the
   watchdog waits `$WaitSeconds` and re-executes. A renewed quota means the next run advances
   (the retry *is* the verification); a still-limited quota fails fast and waits again.

The agent auto-advances sprints: when all batches in the active sprint are `DONE`, it marks the
sprint `DONE`, promotes the next `PENDING` sprint to `ACTIVE`, and continues the loop.

---

## 8. Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Run exits immediately, "no active sprint" | No sprint is `ACTIVE` | Set Sprint 01 to `Status: ACTIVE` in `SPRINTS.md` |
| e2e / integration tests fail with connection errors | Required infrastructure not running | Start services (see §0.3 and `CLAUDE.md`) |
| "worker failed to exit gracefully" warning | Async teardown race (benign) | Ignore — exit code 0 still means pass |
| Run hangs without doing anything | Permission prompt without skip flag | Use `--dangerously-skip-permissions` (§4) |
| Unknown flag error after updating Claude Code | CLI flags changed | `claude --help`, update the script |
| ORM / schema client out of date | Schema edited without regenerating the client | Run the project-specific regenerate command (see `CLAUDE.md`) |
| A batch is BLOCKED on a missing credential | Secret not set in `.env` | Provide the secret, or configure the module to run against a mock/fake |
